{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AptabaseBatchEncoder"}]}]},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Make the destination with "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/aptabase(appKey:host:isDebug:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which fills in the endpoint, the app key’s header field, this encoder and its limits:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let aptabase = try HTTPDestination.aptabase(","    appKey: appKey,  \/\/ from the app's Instructions page: A-EU-…, A-US-… or A-SH-…","    isDebug: false,  \/\/ true for builds whose events only Debug mode should show","    plan: plan)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The body is a JSON array, of content type ","type":"text"},{"code":"application\/json","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", of one event per record, oldest","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"first. Each event is an object of these members:","type":"text"}]},{"header":"row","type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Member"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Holds","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"eventName"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The event’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event\/name"},{"type":"text","text":", as it is"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sessionId"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s session, its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionKey"},{"type":"text","text":", as a lowercase UUID string; the record’s own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/id"},{"type":"text","text":" the same way when its context has no session"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"props"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The event’s stored properties, flattened; left out when there are none"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"systemProps"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The standard context, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isDebug"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sdkVersion"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timestamp"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When the event was tracked, in ISO 8601, in UTC with milliseconds","type":"text"}]}]]]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"systemProps"},{"type":"text","text":" holds "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"osName"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"osVersion"},{"type":"text","text":" from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OperatingSystemKey"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"appVersion"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"appBuildNumber"},{"type":"text","text":" from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ApplicationKey"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deviceModel"},{"type":"text","text":" from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DeviceKey"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"locale"},{"type":"text","text":", the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LocaleKey"},{"type":"text","text":"‘s language and region ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"en-US"},{"type":"text","text":"), each left out when the context has no value for it;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isDebug"},{"type":"text","text":", as the encoder is made with; and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sdkVersion"},{"type":"text","text":", which Aptabase requires, always"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":". A member longer than Aptabase takes (30 characters of the system’s name, 100 of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its version, 50 of the app’s version, 20 of its build and 100 of the device’s model, counted"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in UTF-16) is left out and the event is sent without it, as Aptabase refuses the whole request"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"holding one. The encoder logs a notice the first time it leaves out each member."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The session is the only identifier sent: Aptabase has no member for a user or a device. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record with no session (one tracked by a tracker without ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Enricher.sessions()"},{"text":", or one a store","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"recovered after a relaunch, which keeps no context) is a session of its own: Aptabase takes no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event without a session. The record’s vendor identifier, trace context and other context","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"values aren’t sent. Aptabase counts users itself, from a hash of each request’s IP address and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"User-Agent"},{"text":" header field with a salt it changes every day.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in ","type":"text"},{"code":"plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as ","type":"text"},{"code":"PropertyReader","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reads them. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive","type":"reference"},{"text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals: the property is left","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"out, and so is an element of an array. Aptabase stores a string, a number or a boolean as a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"property’s value, and only a placeholder for an object or array, so an object or array is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"spread into a property per value it holds, named after its path, joined by ","type":"text"},{"code":".","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":"cart.size","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"tags.0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), and a ","type":"text"},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is left out.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out of the request, and the batch’s other records are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sent: one whose event and version "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"type":"text","text":" doesn’t describe; one whose event name is only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whitespace or over 60 characters; one with a property whose name, once flattened, is empty, only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whitespace or over 40 characters, whose string value is over 180 characters, or whose number is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"too large for Aptabase; one whose values flatten to one name; one whose event isn’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"type":"text","text":"; one that holds a value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"JSON can’t; one whose timestamp is outside the years 1 to 9999, or more than 23 hours before"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the batch is encoded; and one too large for a request ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseEncodingError"},{"type":"text","text":")."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"},{"type":"text","text":" returns them as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"type":"text","text":"s, which "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" logs and reports"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dropReports"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" splits a batch into requests within the encoder’s limit, "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default, gives each a deadline 23 hours after its oldest record was tracked, and makes none for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a batch with no record it can write, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" sends nothing for it. Aptabase"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"doesn’t remove duplicates, so a record sent again, after a retry whose answer was lost or a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"store’s redelivery, is counted twice. The bytes are the same for the same records on every run"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and platform: no whitespace, object members in the order of their names’ UTF-8 bytes."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" of Aptabase’s events API, so an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"send events to an Aptabase app’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"POST \/api\/v0\/events"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder\/init(isDebug:plan:limit:now:)"],"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"],"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder\/Failure"],"anchor":"Type-Aliases","title":"Type Aliases"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder\/batchLimit"],"anchor":"Type-Properties","title":"Type Properties"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/aptabaseencoding\/aptabasebatchencoder"]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"AptabaseEncoding"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder.swift#L74","fileName":"AptabaseBatchEncoder.swift"},"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AptabaseBatchEncoder"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","t